1
00:05:04,615 --> 00:05:10,615
Fantasy...beyond your imagination

2
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:15,230
The Lord of the Rings is a adventure, animation,
fantasy film directed by Ralph Bakshi.

3
00:15:13,846 --> 00:15:19,846
Young Hobbit Frodo Baggins is thrown into an amazing adventure when he's tasked
with destroying the One Ring, created by the dark lord Sauron.

4
00:20:18,461 --> 00:20:24,461
Frodo must travel in a small fellowship of nine warriors and accomplices.

5
00:25:23,076 --> 00:25:29,076
But it won't be an easy journey for the Fellowship of the Ring, on
the ultimate quest to rid Middle-earth of evil.

6
00:30:27,692 --> 00:30:33,692
Frodo (voice), played by Christopher Guard.

7
00:35:32,307 --> 00:35:38,307
Gandalf (voice), played by William Squire.

8
00:40:36,923 --> 00:40:42,923
Sam (voice), played by Michael Scholes.

9
00:45:41,538 --> 00:45:47,538
Aragorn (voice), played by John Hurt.

10
00:50:46,153 --> 00:50:52,153
Merry (voice), played by Simon Chandler.

11
00:55:50,769 --> 00:55:56,769
Pippin (voice), played by Dominic Guard.

12
01:00:55,384 --> 01:01:01,384
The Lord of the Rings is a 1978 animated epic fantasy film directed by
Ralph Bakshi from a screenplay by Chris Conkling and Peter S.

13
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It is based on the novel of the same name by J.

14
01:11:04,615 --> 01:11:10,615
Tolkien, adapting from the volumes The Fellowship
of the Ring and The Two Towers.

15
01:16:09,230 --> 01:16:15,230
Set in Middle-earth, the film follows a group of fantasy races—Hobbits, Men, an Elf, a Dwarf and a wizard—who
form a fellowship to destroy a magical ring made by the Dark Lord Sauron, the main antagonist.

16
01:21:13,846 --> 01:21:19,846
Bakshi encountered Tolkien's writing early in his career.

17
01:26:18,461 --> 01:26:24,461
He had made several attempts to produce The Lord of the Rings as an animated film before
producer Saul Zaentz and distributor United Artists provided funding.

18
01:31:23,076 --> 01:31:29,076
The film is notable for its extensive use of rotoscoping, a technique in which
scenes are first shot in live-action, then traced onto animation cels.

19
01:36:27,692 --> 01:36:33,692
It uses a hybrid of traditional cel animation and
rotoscoped live-action footage.

20
01:41:32,307 --> 01:41:38,307
The Lord of the Rings was released in the United States on November
15, 1978, and in the United Kingdom on July 5, 1979.

21
01:46:36,923 --> 01:46:42,923
Although the film received mixed reviews from critics, and hostility from disappointed
viewers who felt that it was incomplete, it was a financial success.

22
01:51:41,538 --> 01:51:47,538
There was no official sequel to cover the remainder of the story.

23
01:56:46,153 --> 01:56:52,153
However, the film has retained a cult following and was a major
inspiration for New Zealand filmmaker Peter Jackson.

24
02:01:50,769 --> 02:01:56,769
The film explores themes of mission, based on
novel or book, elves, dwarf, troll.

25
02:06:55,384 --> 02:07:01,384
The tone is dark.
